---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../site.ts";
---
<Base title="About" description="Who runs the registry, how it is funded, and how to reach us.">
  <article class="prose" data-pagefind-body>
    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
    <h2>Who runs it</h2>
    <p>Because of AI is kept by one editor, <a href="https://davegoldblatt.com" rel="me author">Dave Goldblatt</a> (<a href={`https://x.com/${SITE.editorX}`} rel="me author">@{SITE.editorX}</a> on X), with an automated research run that scans the literature daily and drafts entries from primary sources. Drafted entries publish once the data checks pass and are marked unreviewed until the editor has read the source and confirmed or changed the grades. There is no editorial board.</p>
    <h2>Funding</h2>
    <p>Independent and unfunded. No company, foundation, or model vendor pays for this site or has a say in what it includes.</p>
    <h2>Conflicts</h2>
    <p>Every entry states the conflicts we found: who funded the study, whether the vendor ran it, whether an author works for the company. Where a number comes from a company's own dashboard, the entry says so.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Propose or dispute an entry through the <a href={`${SITE.repo}/issues/new/choose`}>public repository</a>. New entries are posted on X as <a href={`https://x.com/${SITE.x}`} rel="me">@{SITE.x}</a>; the editor is <a href={`https://x.com/${SITE.editorX}`} rel="me">@{SITE.editorX}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
